# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Qloo (the data)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hackathon key: https://docs.qloo.com/reference/qloo-llm-hackathon-developer-guide
# Leave empty to run on built-in demo data.
QLOO_API_KEY=
# Optional; the hackathon base URL is the default.
# QLOO_BASE_URL=https://hackathon.api.qloo.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The planner (the model that chooses the route and writes the words)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick ONE of the three options below. Every city, venue, act and brand in a
# plan comes from Qloo whichever you choose; the model only decides which to
# use and writes the notes and emails.
#
# If both A and B are filled in, A wins. If neither is, C is used.

# --- Option A: any OpenAI-compatible API --------------------------------------
# Works with any provider that offers the /chat/completions API with tool
# calling. Set the base URL, your key, and a model from that provider's list
# that supports tool (function) calling. Common base URLs:
#
#   OpenAI       https://api.openai.com/v1
#   Anthropic    https://api.anthropic.com/v1        (Claude, via Anthropic's OpenAI SDK compatibility)
#   Groq         https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   OpenRouter   https://openrouter.ai/api/v1        (many models behind one key)
#   Together     https://api.together.xyz/v1
#   Mistral      https://api.mistral.ai/v1
#   Ollama       http://localhost:11434/v1           (local models; leave LLM_API_KEY empty)
#   Gemini       https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# --- Option B: Google Gemini (what the hosted demo uses) ----------------------
# Free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest

# --- Option C: no model at all -------------------------------------------------
# Leave A and B empty. A rule-based planner builds the plan from the same Qloo
# data: it picks the best-matched reachable cities, orders the route and fills
# in plain template notes and emails. It is also the automatic fallback if the
# model in A or B is down, rate-limited or too slow.
